diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/parp-experiments.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/parp-experiments.rst
index b86e0cffd..b0c2994b4 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/parp-experiments.rst
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/parp-experiments.rst
@@ -55,4 +55,10 @@ build otherwise matched APPLY images with
 ``CONFIG_PARP_RECLAIM_BIN_SCORE=n/y``.  The ``n`` image preserves native
 random memcg-bin placement and starting-bin selection.
 
+Before accepting a reclaim-bin APPLY round, capture
+``/sys/kernel/debug/parp/reclaim_bin_stats`` before and after the workload.
+The delta of ``scored`` must be positive.  When applications run in child
+systemd scopes below the enabled test slice, ``inherited_hits`` must also grow.
+This prevents a compiled but dormant scorer from being reported as APPLY.
+
 .. lzx-note: pristine Native baseline and build/runtime switch contract.
diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/parp-tier2.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/parp-tier2.rst
index 9989f4e9f..d5d32b126 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/parp-tier2.rst
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/parp-tier2.rst
@@ -23,6 +23,16 @@ only when PARP is in APPLY mode, ``vm.tier2_predict_enabled`` is one, and the
 target cgroup's ``memory.tier2_enabled`` is one.  Otherwise MGLRU uses its
 native random bin placement and random starting bin.
 
+For workloads launched as systemd scopes below an enabled experiment slice,
+the scorer uses the nearest enabled ancestor's Tier2 headroom policy while
+retaining the leaf cgroup for application-prior lookup.  This makes a policy
+set on the test slice cover its dynamically created children without silently
+changing unrelated sibling cgroups.  Runtime coverage is exported in
+``/sys/kernel/debug/parp/reclaim_bin_stats``; in particular, non-zero
+``inherited_hits`` and ``scored`` prove that descendant pages used the scorer.
+
+.. lzx-note: reclaim-bin hierarchy contract and auditable coverage counters.
+
 Watermarks and EWMA
 ===================
 
